/-!
# The classical Hasse surjectivity (NSW (9.2.1), finite-set-of-places form)

`Submission/Work/NUV2/LC/RouteB/twoPlaceRealisation.lean` asks for the *two-place realisation*: for
an open subgroup `U ≤ Gal(K'/K)` fixing a primitive `p`-th root of unity `ζ` (`p` odd) and two
places `A₁, A₂` of `K'` over finite primes of `K` that are not conjugate under `U`, the localisation

  `H²(U, Z/p) → H²(U ⊓ D_{A₁}, Z/p) × H²(U ⊓ D_{A₂}, Z/p)`

is surjective.  This file isolates, as a single `Prop`, the classical theorem which is exactly the
content needed, in the form of a *finite family* of places (the two-place case is the instance
`ι = Fin 2`).

## Mathematical content of `HasseSurj`

Let `F = K'^U` (a number field, since `U` is open, containing `ζ`), so that `H²(U, Z/p)` is the
profinite cohomology `H²(G_F, Z/p) = Br(F)[p]` and `H²(U ⊓ D_A, Z/p) = Br(F_v)[p] ≅ Z/p` for the
place `v` of `F` below `A` (the decomposition group of `A` over `F` is the absolute Galois group of
the completion `F_v`).  The localisation is then the classical localisation
`Br(F)[p] → ∏_{v ∈ S} Br(F_v)[p]` at a finite set `S` of non-archimedean places.

**The theorem.**  This map is surjective for every finite `S`: by the classical exact sequence

  `0 → Br(F) → ⊕_v Br(F_v) → ℚ/ℤ → 0`

(Hasse/Brauer–Hasse–Noether: the localisation is injective and its image is exactly the set of
tuples with `Σ_v inv_v = 0`), a prescribed tuple at `S` is realised by adding the compensating
invariant `-(Σ_{v ∈ S} inv_v)` at one further non-archimedean place `v₀ ∉ S` (there are infinitely
many) and applying the surjectivity of `Br(F) → ker(Σ_v inv_v)`.  In the form used by Neukirch's
argument this is Neukirch's modified surjectivity (NSW (9.2.1)); the labelling by the finite set of
places is essential (the product over *all* places over a prime in the workspace's `NSWSInput` is a
different, stronger statement).

For `p` odd and `ζ_p ∈ F` the archimedean places contribute nothing, so `Z/p`-coefficients agree
with `μ_p` at every level and the statement needs no archimedean bookkeeping.

## Route to a proof (for the prover)

The available unconditional material in this workspace is

* the global fundamental class `NK.GFC.fundamentalClassElement_unconditional`
  (`NK.GlobalCFTdeep.FundamentalClassElement`), hence the cohomological field axiom
  (`NK.GlobalCFTdeep.cohomologicalFieldAxiom_of_fundamentalClassElement`) and Artin reciprocity
  (`NK.GlobalCFTdeep.galoisReciprocity_of_fundamentalClassElement`);
* the local invariant maps `NK.NUV2.LocalInvariant.*` (`Br(M/κ) ≅ ZMod [M : κ]` for a finite
  Galois level of a completion, and the general local-field form);
* Hilbert 90 / Shapiro material for the idèle class group (`NK.HassePrinciple.*`, `H1All`).

What the classical proof consumes and what has to be built:

1. `H²(Γ, C_L) ≅ ℤ/[L:F]` generated by the fundamental class, for finite Galois `L/F` — available;
2. the *local–global compatibility of fundamental classes*: for `w | v`, the image of `u_{L/F}` under
   `H²(Γ, C_L) → H²(Γ_w, C_{L_w})` is the local fundamental class `u_{L_w/F_v}` (Artin–Tate,
   "translation"; the workspace has a first brick in `NK.CFTLib.Translation`), which identifies
   the connecting map `H²(Γ, 𝕀_L) → H²(Γ, C_L)` with the sum `ν` of the local invariants;
3. Hilbert reciprocity, i.e. `ν ∘ (localisation) = 0`, equivalently "a global class cannot be
   ramified at exactly one place"; in this workspace this is the open statement
   `NK.CFTLib.HilbertReciprocityOnePlace` (the single remaining `sorry` of
   `Submission/Work/CFTLib/HR/hilbertReciprocityOnePlace_primePower.lean`; see the docstring there
   for the reduced plan, which uses only the *proved* cyclotomic Artin reciprocity);
4. the index count `|H²(Γ,Lˣ)| = [L:F]`, Chebotarev (a place of local degree `[L:F]`) and Shapiro,
   which turn 2 + 3 into `image = ker ν` at *finite* levels, followed by the passage to the limit
   over the levels (the colimit description of `H2Profinite`).
-/

universe u

open scoped Pointwise

namespace NK.NUV2.LC.RouteB

/-- **The classical Hasse surjectivity at a finite family of places (NSW (9.2.1), finite-set form).**

See the module docstring: for `K` a number field with separable closure `K'`, `p` an odd prime, `ζ`
a primitive `p`-th root of unity fixed by an *open* subgroup `U ≤ Gal(K'/K)`, and a finite family
`A i` of places of `K'` over finite primes of `K` that are pairwise non-conjugate under `U`, the
localisation

  `H²(U, Z/p) → ∏_i H²(U ⊓ D_{A i}, Z/p)`

is surjective.  Equivalently (with `F = K'^U`): every finite family of local Brauer classes of order
dividing `p` over pairwise distinct places of `F` is realised by a global class.

This is the exact input of `NK.NUV2.LC.RouteB.twoPlaceRealisation` (`ι = Fin 2`). -/
def HasseSurj (p : ℕ) (K K' : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field K'] [Algebra K K']
    [IsSepClosure K K'] (ζ : K') : Prop :=
  ∀ (hp : p.Prime) (hodd : p ≠ 2) (hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ p)
    (U : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)) (hUopen : IsOpen (U : Set Gal(K'/K)))
    (hUζ : U ≤ rootFix (K := K) (K' := K') ζ)
    (ι : Type) [Fintype ι] (A : ι → NK.BrauerHasse.OverFinitePrime K K'),
    (∀ i j : ι, i ≠ j → ¬ InOrbit (K := K) (K' := K') U (A i).1 (A j).1) →
    Function.Surjective (fun x : NK.BrauerHasse.H2Profinite (K := K) (K' := K') p U =>
      fun i : ι => NK.BrauerHasse.H2Profinite.loc p U x (A i))

/-- `InOrbit` is symmetric in its two place arguments (conjugation by `v⁻¹`). -/
theorem InOrbit.symm' {K K' : Type u} [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field K'] [Algebra K K']
    [IsSepClosure K K'] {U : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)} {A A' : ValuationSubring K'}
    (h : InOrbit (K := K) (K' := K') U A A') :
    InOrbit (K := K) (K' := K') U A' A := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv, hvA⟩ := h
  refine ⟨v⁻¹, U.inv_mem hv, ?_⟩
  have h2 : v⁻¹ • A' = A := by
    rw [← hvA]
    exact inv_smul_smul v A
  exact h2

end NK.NUV2.LC.RouteB
